# UX-SPEC §3.2 · TESTING-HARNESS.md §3 (`agents.sidebar.row[N]`) — the sidebar's Agents section
# lists the context's native threads with their state, and a click goes to one the way the
# palette's `go` does.
#
# A scripted Codex edit approval leaves one thread blocked on a person. Back in the Hub, its row
# is amber with a `needs you` chip, and a click on it lands on that thread's tab with the
# approval still open.
fixture: agents
await idle
assert targets["agents.sidebar.row[0]"] absent

key o
await screen == Workspace 20000
key ctrl-s A
await agents.threads[0].provider == codex 20000
click agents.composer
type apply the README fix
key enter
await agents.threads[0].pending_gate exists 30000

key ctrl-s s
await screen == Hub 10000
await targets["agents.sidebar.row[0]"] exists 10000
shot sidebar-agents

# Collapsed, the section is dots with tooltips.
key H
await targets["repos.rail"].w == 44
assert targets["agents.sidebar.row[0]"] exists
shot sidebar-agents-collapsed
key H
await targets["repos.rail"].w == 232

click agents.sidebar.row[0]
await screen == Workspace 20000
await mode == Agent 10000
assert agents.threads[0].pending_gate exists && overlay absent
shot sidebar-agent-opened
quit
